   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# ⚗ AlchemicMoss · CALIBRATION\n**Measure YOUR MOSS-Image checkpoint.** Pick it in Load, set the **batch count to 12** next to *Queue*, press *Queue*.\n\nEach run measures one prompt of the list (`line` goes up by one) with the Prompt's negative and **cfg 2.5**, at the resolution of the Prompt (2:3, 1.5 MP). About 50 s per run on a 16 GB GPU. From **8 runs** the profile is reliable: the KSampler's `profile (auto)` finds it by itself and `alchemica_calibrated` and every `-1` value come from it. More runs keep refining it.\n\n`moss_image_sft_int8_convrot` is already calibrated (12 prompts, `profili/`). Calibrate again for `_bf16`, a fine-tune or a LoRA stack (connect it before the Prompt). `mode → replace` starts from scratch.\n\n⚗ Idea & direction: **AlchemicaMente** · code: **Claude (Anthropic)** · [ComfyUI-AlchemicMoss](https://github.com/Nessuno76/ComfyUI-AlchemicMoss) · GPL-3.0"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "### ⚗ Quick guide\n1. **Load** – Krea 2 Turbo + Qwen3-VL text encoder + Qwen-Image VAE.\n2. **LoRA** – up to 6, `(none)` = off.\n3. **Prompt** – write an *idea* (any language): Krea 2's own encoder writes the prompt. `mode → as written` to keep your text. Format: `aspect` + `megapixels`. NAG on = the negative works at cfg 1.\n4. **Sampler** – leave it as is: `profile (auto)` + `alchemica_calibrated` + calibration **v2** use the step spacing measured on your checkpoint. Two stages, resolution-corrected hand-off and **DeGrid** (Krea 2 VAE grid fix) are on.\n5. **Save** – pick drive and folder with 📁 *Browse folders…*; the file takes the workflow's name.\n\n**Tips** · more quality: `steps` 10-12 · more variety between seeds: `variety` 0.6 · strong LoRAs with \"wet\" skin: `variety` 0.15-0.2 · no profile yet? run *⚗ Alchemica Calibration* once on your checkpoint."
   },
   "color": "#2a2a2a",
   "bgcolor": "#1c1c1c"
  },
